  "note": "The room is in writing: The writer you picked writes the whole script.\n\nThe showrunner picked you in the audition. script.md holds your audition pages: keep their voice, and write the whole book.\n\nDrawability: Pages are drawn by an image model, one page per generation, from each character's and location's sheet, and a page drifts when it carries too much. So: at most 4 panels a page; at most 3 named characters in one panel; one location a page where the story allows (every new location needs its own sheet); no crowd that must be recognisable; a big moment gets a splash (one panel, the whole page). Count pages this way, not by comic convention. Every page you make keeps to it.\n\nThe book is exactly 54 pages: pages 1-54, no more, no fewer.\n\nShowrunner's note for this round: Two readers who did not choose this book have read the whole script cold. Their reports are cold-read.md and cold-read-b.md, and each ends every issue with a VERDICT line. The rules are the two in your role guide: nobody puts an issue down on its first page, and everybody wants the next issue. Where a verdict names a put-down page, fix that page, not its wording. Where it says no to the next issue, the last page is not yet a question about a person. Revise the script against both reports; where the two readers disagree, decide, and say why in notes.md.",
